<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Real life: simple versus compound growth of savings (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A youth group in {@town@} has Ksh \( {@P0@} \) to save for \( {@T0@} \) years. Two options are offered, both at \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum:</p>
<ul><li><strong>Plan A</strong> (a SACCO): simple interest.</li><li><strong>Plan B</strong> (a mobile savings app): compound interest, compounded annually.</li></ul>
<p>Give your answers to 2 decimal places where necessary.</p>
<p>(a) Amount after \( {@T0@} \) years with Plan A:</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p>(b) Amount after \( {@T0@} \) years with Plan B:</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p>(c) How much more does Plan B give?</p>
<div>Ksh [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>
<p>(d) Why is there a difference?</p>
<div>[[input:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><strong>(a)</strong> Plan A adds the same \( \frac{ {@R0@} }{100} \times {@P0@} = {@P0*R0/100@} \) every year: \( {@P0@} + {@T0@} \times {@P0*R0/100@} = {@As@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(b)</strong> Plan B multiplies by \( {@float(1 + R0/100)@} \) each year: \( {@P0@} \times ({@float(1 + R0/100)@})^{ {@T0@} } = {@r2(Ac)@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(c)</strong> \( {@r2(Ac)@} - {@As@} = {@r2(Ac - As)@} \).</p>
<p><strong>(d)</strong> In Plan B, each year's interest is added to the balance and then earns interest itself. Simple interest grows in a straight line; compound interest grows faster and faster.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
